I preferred the earlier term, _Basement Nukes_.  Snappier.
> 
> Filthy runs _The (Libertarian) Connection_ (TC), a paper discussion
> group which I would describe as the best thing before the extropians
> list.  A couple of the other extropians came from there and could
> offer opinions.

Agreed.  The Libertarian Connection (edited by Pearson and Shaw) was my
intro to anarchocapitalism when, in 1982, I came across a nearly
complete set of back issues from inception (in late 60s, I think) to mid
70s.  It blew my mind.  Very similar to extropians - this list feels
very much like a continuation of that august publication.  Essentially
the LC printed _anything_ submitted, although the editors would
sometimes comment.  They had the same discussions, strong opinions,
paper flames etc on the Libertarian Party, Objectivism, Rand, proto-PPLs
(called PCs then), drugs, cryonics, smashing the State, uploading,
gender differences, science and philosophy in general etc.

The Libertarian Connection became The Connection under Filthy, sometime
in the mid to late 70s.  The issues I've seen under Filthy seemed to
have lost some of their early lustre and radicalism (although this could
be just that I had accepted and become desensitised to the AC mindset
by then) with stronger editorial control.  For this reason I didn't 
subscribe.  Does Filthy still publish it?  Anyone here subscribe?

